# Changelog

All notable changes to All Blue 22. Versions follow [semantic versioning](https://semver.org/).

## [1.4.1] - 2026-10-12

### Fixed
- Returning players who saved a faction filter before Free Agents existed couldn't find Calvin Hill. New factions now switch on automatically.
- Searching for a character whose faction is switched off now names the faction to turn on, instead of "No characters match".

## [1.4.0] - 2026-10-12

### Added
- Overall rating (OVR) in the 17–0 Challenge and Grand Line Draft. You see how strong a character is overall, but not where they fit best.
- The picker in challenges lists characters strongest first.
- The Grand Line Draft roll card shows the rolled character's OVR.

## [1.3.0] - 2026-10-12

### Changed
- Challenges are now played on instinct. Position fit scores, individual stats and best-fit sorting are hidden while you draft. Every spot on the field shows **?** until the season is played, then the full fits are revealed under Season details.

### Added
- Calvin Hill joins as the first member of the new **Free Agents** faction. He's rated 1 in every attribute and at every position. Good luck.

## [1.2.0] - 2026-10-12

### Added
- **Save image**: turns your lineup or season result into a picture you can download, copy or share.
- **Copy link**: shares your exact lineup. Friends who open it can keep it or go back to their own.
- Link previews: texted and posted links show a title, description and picture of the field.
- Site icon.

## [1.1.0] - 2026-10-12

### Added
- Player portraits: every character gets a badge with their initials, faction color and Devil Fruit pattern. Legends get a gold ring.
- **Player photos**: upload your own picture for any character, one at a time or in bulk by naming files after characters. Photos stay in your browser.

### Changed
- Launched on [allblue22.com](https://allblue22.com).

## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-09

### Added
- **Builder**: draft any character into a 22-player football lineup. Switch between 3-4 and 4-3 defenses and Fullback or Slot offenses, filter by faction, and turn Legends on or off.
- **17–0 Challenge**: each round rolls a faction and a Devil Fruit type. Fill all 22 spots, then play a 17-game season.
- **Grand Line Draft**: each round rolls one random character, with 3 skips per run.
- About 110 characters across 8 factions, each with speed, strength, technique, smarts, toughness and size ratings.
- Position-by-position fit scoring, team score, and a 17-game season against opponents from Loguetown to Laugh Tale.

